@src 1:20
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Mains) 2012
Match List-I with List-II and select the correct answer from the codes given below the lists :
@match
List - I | List - II
A. Anemometer | 1. Earthquakes
B. Seismograph | 2. Atmospheric Pressure
C. Barograph | 3. Wind velocity
D. Hygrometer | 4. Humidity
@endmatch
Code : A B C D
(a) 1 2 3 4
(b) 4 1 2 3
(c) 4 1 3 2
(d) 3 1 2 4
@ans (d)
@end

The **Richter scale** (1935) is logarithmic: each whole number is about **10 times** the ground amplitude and about **32 times** the energy. Seismologists now prefer the **moment magnitude** scale. *Intensity*, the damage felt at a place, is measured on the **Modified Mercalli** scale (I-XII).

